the knowledge base us_statutes_7_2014_c includes:


% 7 U.S.C. 2014(e)(2)(B) — us:statutes/7/2014/e/2/B
the text of "7 USC 2014(e)(2)(B)" is at "sources/us/statutes/7/2014/e/2/B.yaml".

the snap earned income deduction rate is 0.2 if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2008-10-01 <= D.


% 7 U.S.C. 2014(e)(2) — us:statutes/7/2014/e/2
the text of "7 USC 2014(e)(2)" is at "sources/us/statutes/7/2014/e/2.yaml".

rule snap_earned_income_subject_to_deduction with provenance "7 USC 2014(e)(2)":
the snap earned income subject to deduction of a household is an amount N if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2008-10-01 <= D
    and the snap countable earned income of the household is an amount M
    and the work supplementation earned income of the household is an amount K
    and a number P = M - K
    and the maximum of 0 and P is N.

rule snap_earned_income_deduction with provenance "7 USC 2014(e)(2)":
the snap earned income deduction of a household is an amount N if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2008-10-01 <= D
    and the snap earned income subject to deduction of the household is an amount M
        and the snap earned income deduction rate is a rate R
        and N = M * R.


% 7 U.S.C. 2014(e)(6)(A) — us:statutes/7/2014/e/6/A
the text of "7 USC 2014(e)(6)(A)" is at "sources/us/statutes/7/2014/e/6/A.yaml".

the text of "7 USC 2014(d) and (e)" is at "sources/us/statutes/7/2014/e/6/A.yaml".

rule snap_net_income_pre_shelter with provenance "7 USC 2014(e)(6)(A)":
the snap net income pre shelter of a household is an amount N if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2008-10-01 <= D
    and the snap monthly household income of the household is an amount M
    and the snap standard deduction of the household is an amount K
    and the snap earned income deduction of the household is an amount P
    and the dependent care deduction of the household is an amount Q
    and the child support deduction of the household is an amount R
    and the medical deduction of the household is an amount S
    and a number T = M - K - P - Q - R - S
    and the maximum of 0 and T is N.

rule snap_net_income with provenance "7 USC 2014(d) and (e)":
the snap net income of a household is an amount N if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2008-10-01 <= D
    and the snap net income pre shelter of the household is an amount M
    and the snap excess shelter deduction of the household is an amount K
    and a number P = M - K
    and the maximum of 0 and P is N.


% 7 U.S.C. 2014(c) — us:statutes/7/2014/c
the text of "7 USC 2014(c)(2)" is at "sources/us/statutes/7/2014/c.yaml".

the text of "7 USC 2014(c)" is at "sources/us/statutes/7/2014/c.yaml".

the text of "7 USC 2014(c)(1)" is at "sources/us/statutes/7/2014/c.yaml".

the snap gross income excess rate over poverty line is 0.3 if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2008-10-01 <= D.

rule snap_income_standard_poverty_line_with_territory_cap with provenance "7 USC 2014(c)":
the snap income standard poverty line with territory cap of a household is an amount N if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2008-10-01 <= D
    and the household is in virgin islands or guam
        and the poverty line under 42 usc 9902 2 for household area of the household is a code C
        and the poverty line under 42 usc 9902 2 for forty eight contiguous states and dc of the household is a value V
        and the minimum of C and V is N
        otherwise the poverty line under 42 usc 9902 2 for household area of the household is N.

rule snap_net_income_exceeds_poverty_line with provenance "7 USC 2014(c)(1)":
the snap net income of a household exceeds poverty line if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2008-10-01 <= D
    and the snap net income of the household is an amount N
        and the snap income standard poverty line with territory cap of the household is an amount M
        and N > M.

rule household_fails_gross_income_standard with provenance "7 USC 2014(c)(2)":
a household fails gross income standard if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2008-10-01 <= D
    and it is not the case that the household includes elderly or disabled member
    and the snap total gross income of the household is an amount N
    and the snap income standard poverty line with territory cap of the household is an amount M
    and the snap gross income excess rate over poverty line is a rate R
    and N > M * (1 + R).

rule household_ineligible_to_participate_due_to_income_standards_1 with provenance "7 USC 2014(c)":
a household is household ineligible to participate due to income standards if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2008-10-01 <= D
    and the snap net income of the household exceeds poverty line.

rule household_ineligible_to_participate_due_to_income_standards_2 with provenance "7 USC 2014(c)":
a household is household ineligible to participate due to income standards if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2008-10-01 <= D
    and the household fails gross income standard.

